# Act 1, chapter 1 "Red Ribbon Science" - opening in Gero's lab (replaces Buu's Fury's Snake Way opening).
# Original steps kept: 1 = scene setup, 3 = (type 4 data), 5 = camera, 15 = journal flag, 17 = hand control back.
# 'do' lines are script code: begin_moves / move <actor> x y / wait_moves / face <actor> dir (0 down, 1 up, 2 side).
replace 0x780550
keep 1
narrate Red Ribbon Army Headquarters. Deep beneath the command tower, the army's chief scientist was still at work.
# step 3 (BF's packed Snake Way setup) walked the player in from the map edge through the wall; load the lab with
# Gero already at his bench instead (the field-return idiom: step 1 has done 115/121/165)
do call 120 1; call 119 1 1 1 112 200; call 121 60
say young_gero.0 The drone's targeting array is drifting again...
say young_gero.0 Three degrees off true. Three degrees is the difference between a hit and a wasted shell.
keep 5
say gevo.0 Father! You haven't left this lab in three days. Commander Red wants the drone report by morning.
do begin_moves; move gevo 96 176; wait_moves; face gevo 2
say young_gero.0 Then Commander Red will have it by morning, Gevo. Perfection takes time. The army can wait one more night.
say gevo.0 The army can't wait. My squad ships out to the Northern Wastelands at dawn.{p}They say some kid with a staff has been tearing through our outposts.
say young_gero.1 A child? The Red Ribbon Army is afraid of a child?{p}Take two of my drones with you. I'll guide them from right here in the lab.
say gevo.2 You and your machines...
say gevo.0 All right. But promise me you'll get some sleep.
say young_gero.0 I'll sleep when my work is finished. Now go, Gevo. And come back in one piece.
say gevo.0 I always do. And don't forget the {c07}drone terminal{c02}. Commander Red wants that report.
# Gevo leaves through the tank-room door: walk to it, open the door panels (tools/doors.py states: a sideways nudge =
# half open, up = open), walk into the doorway, then fade and swap to 1:61 (the same lab without Gevo)
do begin_moves; move gevo 81 182; wait_moves
do begin_moves; move door_540fd4_0_0 80 126; move door_540fd4_0_1 80 128; wait_moves; call 136 5; begin_moves; move door_540fd4_0_0 80 125; move door_540fd4_0_1 80 127; wait_moves
do begin_moves; move gevo 81 146; wait_moves
do call 120 30
do call 119 1 61 1 112 200; call 121 30
say young_gero.0 Hmph. Always telling me what to do... just like his mother.
keep 15
journal Check the {c07}drone terminal{c02}
keep 17
do call 165 0 15; call 165 0 14
